2026-11-07T05:45:12.0392447Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0402285Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0403015Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0403558Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0403843Z 
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0404037Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0404508Z 
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0404752Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0405273Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0405548Z 
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0405677Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0406013Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0406246Z 
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0406485Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T05:45:12.0406933Z   $ sh ./install-nix
